Drain / shutdown directive acceptance and true effect
====================================================
1) `totally_bogus_zzz 1s;` inside http{} — is unknown-directive validation present?
   61cc738c  rc=1  /tmp/tb.conf:2: unknown directive totally_bogus_zzz
   44bf7f35  rc=1  config: /tmp/tb.conf:2: unknown http directive totally_bogus_zzz
   063b0d5e  rc=0  ******** silently accepted
   8d5ff1f2  rc=0  ******** silently accepted
   29d05850  rc=0  ******** silently accepted
   6fb186ed  rc=0  ******** silently accepted

2) `toksec_drain_timeout 5s;` in http{} — accepted by all six (spec scope), so acceptance
   is not evidence of implementation.

3) Source use of the value:
   063b0d5e  grep toksec_drain_timeout -> 0 hits
   29d05850  grep toksec_drain_timeout -> 0 hits
   6fb186ed  grep toksec_drain_timeout -> 0 hits
   8d5ff1f2  1 hit, line 67, inside the "allowed names" set only:
             "toksec_drain_timeout" appears in the string set that validates the spelling;
             no further reference exists in the file.

4) Shutdown path in all four is a fixed worker SIGTERM followed by an unbounded waitpid,
   with the configured deadline never consulted:
   8d5ff1f2 line 98   for(auto p:workers)kill(p,SIGTERM);
                      for(auto p:workers)waitpid(p,nullptr,0)
   29d05850 line 60   for(pid_t p:workers)kill(p,SIGTERM);
                      for(pid_t p:workers)waitpid(p,nullptr,0)
   6fb186ed line 75   for(pid_t p:kills)kill(p,SIGTERM);   (kids)
                      for(pid_t p:kids)waitpid(p,nullptr,0)
   063b0d5e line 82   for(auto p:children)kill(p,SIGTERM);
                      while(waitpid(-1,nullptr,0)>0){}

5) Behaviour with `toksec_drain_timeout 5s;` set and a 2.0 s upstream delay:
   all of 8d5ff1f2 / 29d05850 / 6fb186ed returned EOF at +0.00 s with 0 of 10 body bytes,
   master exited at +0.25 s — a 5 s deadline never used.
